IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssa-common`
IMPORT `ssa-figures`

-- Social Security Act, the Medicare entitlement and enrollment basics: Part A (hospital insurance) entitlement at 65 and on
-- disability (s 426(a), (b), (h)), and enrollment in Part A for the otherwise uninsured (s 1395i-2(a)); Part B (supplementary
-- medical insurance) eligibility (s 1395o(a)), the initial, general and special enrollment periods and deemed enrollment
-- (s 1395p(d)-(g), (i)), when coverage begins (s 1395q(a)), and the standard premium with the late-enrollment increase
-- (s 1395r(a)(3), (b)).
--
-- Edition: s 426 from ../../registers/source-bundle/usc42-ch7-schII.txt; ss 1395c-1395r from usc42-ch7-schXVIII-eligibility.txt
-- (OLRC USLM, release point Public Law 119-121). Figures: ssa-figures.l4 (2026 Part B premium, 90 FR 52063).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medicare -- Part A entitlement and Part B enrollment`

§§ `s 426(a) -- Part A at age 65`

-- s 426(a): "Every individual who (1) has attained age 65, and (2)(A) is entitled to monthly insurance benefits under section
-- 402 ..., would be entitled to those benefits except that he has not filed an application therefor ..., and ... files an
-- application for hospital insurance benefits ..., (B) is a qualified railroad retirement beneficiary, or (C) would meet the
-- requirements of subparagraph (A) ... if medicare qualified government employment ... were treated as employment ... and
-- files an application ... shall be entitled to hospital insurance benefits". NOTES.md finding 12: "files an application" is
-- read as the condition for the not-yet-entitled limbs only; a person already entitled to s 402 benefits needs no separate
-- application.
GIVEN `has attained age 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is entitled to monthly insurance benefits under s 402` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would be entitled to s 402 benefits on filing an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a qualified railroad retirement beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would be so entitled if medicare qualified government employment were counted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has filed an application for hospital insurance benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to hospital insurance benefits under s 426(a)` IF
        `has attained age 65`
    AND (    `is entitled to monthly insurance benefits under s 402`
         OR (`would be entitled to s 402 benefits on filing an application` AND `has filed an application for hospital insurance benefits`)
         OR `is a qualified railroad retirement beneficiary`
         OR (`would be so entitled if medicare qualified government employment were counted` AND `has filed an application for hospital insurance benefits`))

§§ `s 426(b), (h) -- Part A on disability`

-- s 426(b): under 65 and "entitled to, and has for 24 calendar months been entitled to, (i) disability insurance benefits ...
-- or (ii) child's insurance benefits ... by reason of a disability ... or (iii) widow's ... or widower's insurance benefits
-- ... by reason of a disability", entitled "beginning with ... the twenty-fifth month of his entitlement", ending with the
-- month before age 65 (when s 426(a) takes over). s 426(h): with ALS, "the first month (rather than twenty-fifth month) of
-- entitlement". s 426(f) (months of an earlier period counted) is not encoded.
GIVEN `first month of entitlement to the disability benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `has been medically determined to have ALS` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month of hospital insurance on disability` `first month of entitlement to the disability benefit` `has been medically determined to have ALS` MEANS
    IF `has been medically determined to have ALS`
        THEN `first month of entitlement to the disability benefit`
        ELSE `first month of entitlement to the disability benefit` PLUS 24

§§ `s 1395i-2(a) -- buying Part A`

-- s 1395i-2(a): an individual who "(1) has attained the age of 65, (2) is enrolled under part B ..., (3) is a resident of the
-- United States, and is either (A) a citizen or (B) an alien lawfully admitted for permanent residence who has resided in the
-- United States continuously during the 5 years immediately preceding the month in which he applies ..., and (4) is not
-- otherwise entitled to benefits under this part" may enroll in Part A (with a premium under s 1395i-2(d), not deposited
-- for 2026).
GIVEN `has attained age 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is enrolled under Part B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a resident and a citizen, or a permanent resident with 5 years' continuous residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is otherwise entitled to Part A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may enroll in Part A under s 1395i-2` IF
        `has attained age 65`
    AND `is enrolled under Part B`
    AND `is a resident and a citizen, or a permanent resident with 5 years' continuous residence`
    AND NOT `is otherwise entitled to Part A`

§§ `s 1395o(a) -- who may enroll in Part B`

-- s 1395o(a): "(1) is entitled to hospital insurance benefits under part A, or (2) has attained age 65 and is a resident of
-- the United States, and is either (A) a citizen or (B) an alien lawfully admitted for permanent residence who has resided in
-- the United States continuously during the 5 years immediately preceding the month in which he applies".
GIVEN `is entitled to Part A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has attained age 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a resident and a citizen, or a permanent resident with 5 years' continuous residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible to enroll in Part B` IF
        `is entitled to Part A`
    OR (`has attained age 65` AND `is a resident and a citizen, or a permanent resident with 5 years' continuous residence`)

§§ `s 1395p -- enrollment periods`

-- s 1395p(d): the initial enrollment period "shall begin on the first day of the third month before the month in which he
-- first satisfies [s 1395o(a)(1) or (2)] and shall end seven months later": the three months before, that month, and the
-- three after.
GIVEN `month first eligible to enroll` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month of the initial enrollment period` `month first eligible to enroll` MEANS `month first eligible to enroll` MINUS 3

GIVEN `month first eligible to enroll` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last month of the initial enrollment period` `month first eligible to enroll` MEANS `month first eligible to enroll` PLUS 3

-- s 1395p(e): "a general enrollment period during the period beginning on January 1 and ending on March 31 of each year".
GIVEN `month number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in a general enrollment period` IF
    (`month number` MINUS 12 TIMES (`the year of month number` `month number`)) AT MOST 2

-- s 1395p(f): deemed enrolled if eligible by reason of Part A entitlement, the initial enrollment period begins after March
-- 1973, and "residing in the United States, exclusive of Puerto Rico". (The right to decline, in regulations, is not in the
-- deposited text.)
GIVEN `is eligible by reason of entitlement to Part A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first month of the initial enrollment period` IS A NUMBER
      `resides in the United States, not in Puerto Rico` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is deemed enrolled in Part B` IF
        `is eligible by reason of entitlement to Part A`
    AND `first month of the initial enrollment period` GREATER THAN `the month number of` 1973 3
    AND `resides in the United States, not in Puerto Rico`

-- s 1395p(d): a permission to enroll in the seven months of the initial enrollment period, in months from its first month.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `SSA party` `SSA act`
`s 1395p(d) -- the individual may enroll in Part B during the seven-month initial enrollment period` MEANS
    PARTY `the individual`
    MAY   `enroll in Part B`
    WITHIN 7

-- s 1395p(i)(1), (3)(A): a person who was in a group health plan "by reason of the individual's (or the individual's
-- spouse's) current employment status" when first eligible and did not enroll has a special enrollment period that includes
-- each month of that coverage and ends "with the last day of the eighth consecutive month in which the individual is at no
-- time so enrolled". In months from the end of that coverage.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `SSA party` `SSA act`
`s 1395p(i) -- after employer group health coverage ends, the individual may enroll in Part B within eight months` MEANS
    PARTY `the individual`
    MAY   `enroll in Part B`
    WITHIN 8

§§ `s 1395q(a) -- when Part B coverage begins`

DECLARE `Part B enrollment` IS ONE OF
    `enrolled in the initial enrollment period`
    `deemed enrolled`
    `enrolled in a general enrollment period`

-- s 1395q(a)(2)(A): enrolled in the initial period before the month first eligible -- "the first day of such month";
-- (2)(C): first eligible on or after 1 January 2023 and enrolled in that month or later in the initial period -- "the first
-- day of the month following the month in which he so enrolls"; (2)(D)(ii): enrolled in a general enrollment period from
-- 2023 -- the month after enrolling; (3)(A): deemed enrolled by the third month of the initial period (s 1395p(g)(2)(A)
-- deems it in that month for those already on s 402 or s 423 benefits) -- the month first eligible. Months before 2023 are
-- not encoded (the old (2)(B) and (D)(i) rules).
GIVEN `how enrolled` IS A `Part B enrollment`
      `month first eligible to enroll` IS A NUMBER
      `month of enrollment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month of Part B coverage` `how enrolled` `month first eligible to enroll` `month of enrollment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how enrolled`
    WHEN `enrolled in the initial enrollment period` THEN
        IF `month of enrollment` LESS THAN `month first eligible to enroll`
            THEN `month first eligible to enroll`
            ELSE `month of enrollment` PLUS 1
    WHEN `deemed enrolled` THEN
        IF `month of enrollment` AT MOST (`the first month of the initial enrollment period` `month first eligible to enroll` PLUS 2)
            THEN `month first eligible to enroll`
            ELSE `month of enrollment` PLUS 1
    WHEN `enrolled in a general enrollment period` THEN `month of enrollment` PLUS 1

§§ `s 1395r -- the premium and the late-enrollment increase`

-- s 1395r(b): enrolled after the initial enrollment period, and not in a special period under s 1395p(i)(4), (l) or (m), "the
-- monthly premium ... shall be increased by 10 percent of the monthly premium so determined for each full 12 months ... in
-- which he could have been but was not enrolled", counting "the months which elapsed between the close of his initial
-- enrollment period and the close of the enrollment period in which he enrolled" (and, on re-enrollment, from the end of the
-- earlier coverage), but not months in an employer group health plan by reason of current employment.
GIVEN `months between the close of the initial period and the close of the period of enrollment` IS A NUMBER
      `of those, months in an employer group health plan by reason of current employment` IS A NUMBER
      `enrolled in a special period under s 1395p(i)(4), (l) or (m)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full 12-month periods of late enrollment` `months between the close of the initial period and the close of the period of enrollment` `of those, months in an employer group health plan by reason of current employment` `enrolled in a special period under s 1395p(i)(4), (l) or (m)` MEANS
    IF `enrolled in a special period under s 1395p(i)(4), (l) or (m)`
        THEN 0
        ELSE FLOOR ((max 0 (`months between the close of the initial period and the close of the period of enrollment` MINUS `of those, months in an employer group health plan by reason of current employment`)) DIVIDED BY 12)

-- s 1395r(a)(2)-(3): the monthly premium is the promulgated rate (2026: $202.90), adjusted under (b). The income-related
-- adjustment of s 1395r(i) is not encoded. NOTES.md finding 13: (b) does not say how the increase is rounded; it is left
-- unrounded.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `full 12-month periods of late enrollment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the monthly Part B premium` `calendar year` `full 12-month periods of late enrollment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures for` `calendar year`
    WHEN JUST f THEN `answered` (f's `standard monthly Part B premium` PLUS f's `standard monthly Part B premium` TIMES 0.10 TIMES `full 12-month periods of late enrollment`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the figures the Act needs for that year are not deposited: only the 2026 Federal Register notices are`
